WEBVTT

00:00:01.130 --> 00:00:04.370
Sorry to call you in so late at night.

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:06.650
Oh, we don't mind at all.

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:08.150
Did something happen?

00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:12.280
Actually, there's something 
I want to tell you.

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:24.120
That's a lot of stuff.

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:28.040
I'm sure Sana-chan will be hungry,

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:31.010
so I brought lots of her favorite foods.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:33.260
I see.

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:36.790
I've already informed our clients,

00:00:36.790 --> 00:00:39.790
but I'll need you two to watch 
the shop while I'm away.

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:40.980
Can you do that?

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:42.190
Of course!

00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:43.380
No problem.

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:44.360
Thanks.

00:00:45.890 --> 00:00:47.850
Oh, he's back.

00:00:53.690 --> 00:00:54.700
All right!

00:02:24.990 --> 00:02:30.000
<b>The Queen and the Witch</b>

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.840
<b>No Service</b>

00:02:30.690 --> 00:02:32.840
No good. There's no service.

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:35.820
"No service"? The thing that 
happens underground?

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:36.530
Yeah.

00:02:36.530 --> 00:02:38.840
I've never actually seen it before.

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:43.620
I think we're in the deepest 
part of Wonderland.

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:47.640
We fell from up there, right?

00:02:48.190 --> 00:02:49.330
I think so...

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:53.450
Then, if we go up, we can get 
back to that last door, right?

00:02:55.370 --> 00:02:56.660
I don't know.

00:02:57.390 --> 00:02:58.320
What do you mean?

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:00.010
You know, don't you?

00:03:00.010 --> 00:03:02.020
Don't be mean! Just tell me!

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:04.640
I really don't know.

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:08.270
I can't use the power 
that I normally use,

00:03:08.270 --> 00:03:12.110
and I've never been to this part 
of Wonderland, either...

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:21.380
Where are you going?

00:03:21.380 --> 00:03:24.410
Where else? To look for the exit.

00:03:24.410 --> 00:03:26.190
I don't think that'll work!

00:03:27.090 --> 00:03:28.140
Hey!

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:29.180
You're kidding, right?

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:30.850
You'll get tired!

00:03:40.250 --> 00:03:42.040
Wait for me!

00:03:49.470 --> 00:03:50.450
Hey!

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:53.170
Wait...

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:02.300
I told them everything.

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:05.730
Including where Sana came from

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:08.510
and what kind of power she has.

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:09.430
Sorry.

00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:13.460
I know Naito told us to keep 
it as quiet as possible.

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:16.300
In this situation, you had no choice.

00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:18.270
They must have been surprised, right?

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:22.370
Nah, seems they already had a hunch...

00:04:22.370 --> 00:04:23.780
What did they say?

00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:25.900
Hardly anything.

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:28.030
"Sana-chan is Sana-chan, isn't she?"

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:29.110
That's it.

00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:31.820
I'm sure that would make 
Sana-chan happy.

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:54.320
Hey! It'll never work!

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:04.490
Sana-chan was born in Wonderland,

00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:06.570
but we still don't know much about it.

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:09.110
Please be very careful, both of you.

00:05:09.110 --> 00:05:10.360
Wow...

00:05:10.360 --> 00:05:13.870
But the name sounds like an 
amusement park, doesn't it?

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:16.980
Are you worried?

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:19.770
What about you?

00:05:22.460 --> 00:05:25.510
When Sana-chan was taken before,

00:05:25.510 --> 00:05:28.390
I was really worried.

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:31.200
But ultimately, it all 
worked out, didn't it?

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:34.290
So I've decided that it'll 
be okay this time, too.

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:36.540
I see.

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:37.440
Besides,

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:40.720
I'm the alien of happy endings!

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:44.780
But that time, Naito-san was 
the one driving...

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:47.280
Oh! Would you have preferred Naito?

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:49.550
Nope, I prefer you.

00:05:49.550 --> 00:05:50.780
That's a relief.

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:31.540
Mom!

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:45.310
<i>No...</i>

00:06:46.220 --> 00:06:48.720
I told you... it wouldn't work.

00:06:49.630 --> 00:06:52.900
Since my power is gone,

00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:54.970
I think the exit disappeared...

00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:55.800
That can't be.

00:06:55.800 --> 00:06:58.390
I have to stay with my mom forever!

00:06:58.390 --> 00:07:00.180
Send me home, right now!

00:07:00.180 --> 00:07:04.250
I... I want to go home, too.

00:07:08.830 --> 00:07:11.110
I don't think anyone's there!

00:07:12.580 --> 00:07:15.380
I'm telling the truth...

00:07:16.420 --> 00:07:18.050
We believe the girl

00:07:18.050 --> 00:07:21.010
with Sana-chan was responsible 
for the Harajuku incident.

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:21.540
<b>Imai Pharmaceutical Corporation</b>

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:25.630
There's no cell signal where they 
are, so we lack detailed intel.

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:29.690
Wonderland is constantly changing.

00:07:29.690 --> 00:07:33.890
But since we confirmed they're 
both there, we've been unable

00:07:33.890 --> 00:07:36.220
to learn anything going on inside.

00:07:36.220 --> 00:07:39.380
It's possible that we could encounter
 unpredictable dangers,

00:07:39.380 --> 00:07:42.060
so please be very careful.

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:44.860
We still can't see it?

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:47.270
We can verify there's a 
signal, but that's all.

00:07:47.270 --> 00:07:49.580
The energy signal coming 
from inside is stronger.

00:07:49.580 --> 00:07:51.060
Does that mean it's expanding?

00:07:51.060 --> 00:07:51.960
Most likely.

00:07:51.960 --> 00:07:53.060
Will it affect this world?

00:07:53.060 --> 00:07:54.030
Trying to calculate that now.

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:57.740
<i>Please enter your twelve-digit passcode.</i>

00:08:06.540 --> 00:08:09.960
So this is where Sana-chan was born?

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:12.850
And those two girls are 
in here, somewhere?

00:08:12.850 --> 00:08:13.630
Yes.

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:17.050
Senpai!

00:08:19.190 --> 00:08:22.500
That form is just the best...

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:24.400
Yamada, what is your job?

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:26.240
To back you up,

00:08:26.240 --> 00:08:28.850
and to collect data on Wonderland!

00:08:28.850 --> 00:08:30.430
Good, as long as you know that.

00:08:31.070 --> 00:08:32.530
Wait, Grandpa!

00:08:32.530 --> 00:08:34.030
Kashimura-san, please wait!

00:08:40.530 --> 00:08:44.120
Excuse me! Is anyone here?

00:08:44.380 --> 00:08:47.380
If so, please answer me!

00:08:48.140 --> 00:08:50.880
Is anyone here?

00:09:09.210 --> 00:09:11.190
What's wrong, Grandpa?

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:13.930
That's Sana-chan...

00:09:13.930 --> 00:09:18.010
with Asahi-chan and 
Yonaga-chan, isn't it?

00:09:24.510 --> 00:09:25.920
Is that...

00:09:26.470 --> 00:09:29.470
the stuffed pig I bought for her?

00:09:32.130 --> 00:09:34.630
Oh! The spotted pig!

00:09:34.630 --> 00:09:38.580
I bet if we follow that pig, 
we'll find Sana-chan!

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:40.450
Isn't that a shot in the dark?

00:09:40.450 --> 00:09:42.400
Huh? Is it?

00:09:42.840 --> 00:09:44.500
Seems it's our only choice.

00:09:44.870 --> 00:09:45.850
Right?

00:09:45.850 --> 00:09:47.940
Maybe we should consider this further.

00:09:48.300 --> 00:09:50.490
Kashimura-san? Kashimura-san!

00:09:54.450 --> 00:09:57.400
Is this another of Sana's memories?

00:09:58.420 --> 00:10:00.050
No idea.

00:10:00.050 --> 00:10:01.580
I'll take a look from above.

00:10:02.510 --> 00:10:03.830
#41.

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:05.050
Huh?

00:10:05.410 --> 00:10:06.200
What?!

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:07.290
Ichijo-san?

00:10:30.070 --> 00:10:31.180
Sorry.

00:10:35.310 --> 00:10:38.290
I was only trying to get you
guys back for what happened.

00:10:38.290 --> 00:10:40.910
I had no idea we'd get stuck here.

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:45.160
Sorry. This is all my fault.

00:10:45.160 --> 00:10:46.930
I'm really sorry.

00:10:52.640 --> 00:10:53.740
No...

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:57.840
This might have been my doing.

00:10:58.510 --> 00:10:59.970
Hey, Grandpa...

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:02.310
Do you think Ichijo-san is okay?

00:11:02.310 --> 00:11:05.050
Aren't you a happy alien?

00:11:05.050 --> 00:11:05.930
Huh?

00:11:06.460 --> 00:11:07.770
Aren't you?

00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:09.980
Yeah!

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:12.560
Ichijo-san's really strong, isn't she?

00:11:12.980 --> 00:11:15.270
Yeah, she sure is.

00:11:27.580 --> 00:11:28.670
What the?

00:11:28.670 --> 00:11:31.160
It's almost like someone's mocking us.

00:11:32.290 --> 00:11:36.660
Later, I'll have to give this 
Wonderland place a talking to.

00:11:36.660 --> 00:11:37.880
Wow!

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:41.220
You're gonna give Wonderland a lecture!

00:11:44.520 --> 00:11:46.480
Hey, what is that?

00:11:46.800 --> 00:11:49.300
I think it's practicing.

00:11:50.650 --> 00:11:52.780
Practicing what?

00:11:52.780 --> 00:11:54.350
Things it's learned.

00:11:54.350 --> 00:11:55.850
Things it's learned?

00:11:56.510 --> 00:11:58.730
Wonderland wants to know

00:11:59.370 --> 00:12:01.950
what the world is made of.

00:12:02.300 --> 00:12:04.950
Not just things like colors, shapes,

00:12:04.950 --> 00:12:08.250
smells, and flavors...

00:12:08.740 --> 00:12:11.610
I think it wants to know 
about all its rules.

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:15.840
Like the kinds of mechanisms 
that make it up,

00:12:16.250 --> 00:12:19.360
what life is made of,

00:12:19.720 --> 00:12:23.740
and how humans see the world.

00:12:23.740 --> 00:12:27.220
I think it gathers all of those 
things from our world,

00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:29.180
and it imitates them.

00:12:29.680 --> 00:12:31.980
Maybe the Mirror Gates

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:36.370
are the peepholes that 
Wonderland uses to do that.

00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:44.860
At first, I think Wonderland
was just a bit larger than this room.

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:48.620
But eventually, I think it'll 
become a whole universe.

00:12:50.060 --> 00:12:51.270
Strange...

00:12:53.230 --> 00:12:58.840
Everything you say is so unbelievable,

00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:02.090
but for some reason, 
I don't think you're lying.

00:13:03.710 --> 00:13:05.590
You're a mysterious girl.

00:13:05.950 --> 00:13:07.320
I'm not weird!

00:13:07.760 --> 00:13:09.430
I didn't say you were weird.

00:13:09.800 --> 00:13:11.220
I'm not lying!

00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:12.970
I didn't say you were lying, either.

00:13:12.970 --> 00:13:14.290
You're so funny.

00:13:14.290 --> 00:13:15.680
I'm not funny!

00:13:16.830 --> 00:13:21.250
Then, wouldn't this world 
have to have thought

00:13:21.250 --> 00:13:22.810
of something amazing?

00:13:24.100 --> 00:13:28.500
It's really weird and beyond 
my comprehension,

00:13:28.960 --> 00:13:30.280
but it's beautiful.

00:13:32.070 --> 00:13:33.750
If this world

00:13:34.530 --> 00:13:37.480
will eventually become a different one,

00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:42.210
then maybe I could just 
live here forever.

00:13:45.370 --> 00:13:48.680
I've succeeded in running away...

00:13:49.250 --> 00:13:51.580
Are you sure about that?

00:13:52.480 --> 00:13:53.780
About what?

00:13:54.850 --> 00:13:56.100
Uh...

00:13:56.100 --> 00:13:58.890
But if you stay here forever, 
you'll be bored!

00:13:58.890 --> 00:14:02.780
And didn't you say you wanted 
to go back to your mom?!

00:14:02.780 --> 00:14:05.790
Leave me alone. 
You wouldn't understand.

00:14:15.720 --> 00:14:16.910
I'm sorry.

00:14:18.050 --> 00:14:20.530
That was a mean thing to say.

00:14:23.170 --> 00:14:25.300
I'm not sure where to start.

00:14:27.580 --> 00:14:31.540
You see, my mom hates me.

00:14:31.540 --> 00:14:34.760
By "mom," do you mean your mother?

00:14:34.760 --> 00:14:36.140
That's right.

00:14:36.820 --> 00:14:37.810
I see...

00:14:37.810 --> 00:14:40.030
My Sanae has a mother, too,

00:14:40.030 --> 00:14:42.570
and that mother's father is Zoroku.

00:14:42.570 --> 00:14:45.570
But I don't have either, 
so I don't really get it.

00:14:45.920 --> 00:14:47.290
Really?

00:14:47.290 --> 00:14:48.070
Yeah.

00:14:54.350 --> 00:14:57.660
Hey... Can I tell you something?

00:14:58.300 --> 00:14:59.080
Okay.

00:14:59.560 --> 00:15:01.480
My parents have been

00:15:01.480 --> 00:15:04.590
fighting for many years now.

00:15:04.970 --> 00:15:06.300
Why?

00:15:06.300 --> 00:15:09.090
I failed my elementary 
school entrance exam,

00:15:09.090 --> 00:15:11.560
and I disappointed my mom.

00:15:14.420 --> 00:15:18.770
Ever since then, Mom won't 
even look me in the eye.

00:15:19.310 --> 00:15:22.730
So I think it's best if I'm not there.

00:15:23.150 --> 00:15:26.710
That way, Mom and Dad won't fight,

00:15:26.710 --> 00:15:28.890
and they can always be happy.

00:15:33.110 --> 00:15:36.040
Also, sometimes Mom looks at me

00:15:36.040 --> 00:15:41.080
as if she's looking in from a 
universe of endless darkness.

00:15:42.870 --> 00:15:45.840
When I see her like that, I think...

00:15:47.110 --> 00:15:50.250
I love my mom...

00:15:51.030 --> 00:15:56.590
But she probably wishes 
I weren't her daughter...

00:16:01.980 --> 00:16:05.540
I... don't want to go home!

00:16:05.540 --> 00:16:08.670
I should never have existed at all.

00:16:16.910 --> 00:16:18.560
H-Hey...

00:16:19.390 --> 00:16:21.860
This might make you mad.

00:16:25.400 --> 00:16:28.590
But I think it's okay that you exist.

00:16:33.840 --> 00:16:35.000
Thanks.

00:16:35.610 --> 00:16:36.760
That's wrong.

00:16:38.070 --> 00:16:42.040
I don't think there's anyone

00:16:42.040 --> 00:16:45.150
who should or shouldn't exist.

00:16:45.150 --> 00:16:49.730
That's why it scares me to 
think about those things...

00:16:51.530 --> 00:16:53.430
You know...

00:16:54.070 --> 00:16:55.760
I was born here.

00:16:57.400 --> 00:17:00.260
I'm not human, like everyone else.

00:17:00.260 --> 00:17:04.580
I think I'm Wonderland itself.

00:17:12.060 --> 00:17:13.540
That's it for practice!

00:17:13.540 --> 00:17:15.130
Thank you!

00:17:15.130 --> 00:17:16.300
Wanna go somewhere?

00:17:16.300 --> 00:17:16.990
Ice cream!

00:17:16.990 --> 00:17:17.680
Okay.

00:17:17.680 --> 00:17:19.280
Oh, I've got cram school now.

00:17:18.210 --> 00:17:23.580
<i>The number you have dialed is 
out of the service area or—</i>

00:17:24.930 --> 00:17:27.400
<b>Ha-chan</b>

00:17:24.930 --> 00:17:27.400
<b>No Answer</b>

00:17:26.120 --> 00:17:27.400
Ha-chan...

00:17:27.970 --> 00:17:29.770
Not human?

00:17:29.770 --> 00:17:30.570
Yeah.

00:17:32.360 --> 00:17:33.950
H-Huh?

00:17:33.950 --> 00:17:36.450
W-Wait, what are you...

00:17:38.470 --> 00:17:40.440
L-Listen...

00:17:40.440 --> 00:17:44.330
The truth is that I was told not 
to tell anyone about this.

00:17:44.940 --> 00:17:49.040
But when I was first born here, 
I was something else...

00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:51.750
Something I can't explain.

00:17:51.750 --> 00:17:54.340
I don't think I was even 
shaped like a human.

00:17:54.840 --> 00:17:58.500
Then, before I knew it, 
I had eyes and a body,

00:17:58.500 --> 00:18:00.010
and I looked like this.

00:18:00.690 --> 00:18:04.600
But I'm pretty sure I was 
a part of Wonderland.

00:18:05.960 --> 00:18:07.630
You don't believe me?

00:18:07.630 --> 00:18:10.470
No, I'm just surprised.

00:18:10.470 --> 00:18:12.940
I figured it out after hearing about you.

00:18:12.940 --> 00:18:16.390
I was similar, and it made me 
frazzled for a long time.

00:18:16.940 --> 00:18:18.100
I'm pretty sure

00:18:18.100 --> 00:18:21.240
I'm still connected to this place, somehow.

00:18:21.620 --> 00:18:25.080
But the outside world and 
real humans are what

00:18:25.080 --> 00:18:27.240
Wonderland wants to know about.

00:18:27.240 --> 00:18:30.810
So I'm just something like 
a communication device.

00:18:30.810 --> 00:18:34.540
But if that's true, many others 
could take my place.

00:18:34.540 --> 00:18:37.430
Maybe my existence isn't really necessary,

00:18:37.430 --> 00:18:40.000
and I don't matter at all...

00:18:42.010 --> 00:18:45.820
Maybe it's wrong for me 
to care about anyone,

00:18:45.820 --> 00:18:49.840
and I'm actually someone 
who isn't needed.

00:18:57.720 --> 00:18:59.270
U-Uh, I mean...

00:18:59.270 --> 00:19:02.630
I don't have a mom, 
so maybe you don't like

00:19:02.630 --> 00:19:04.800
my comparing myself to you!

00:19:06.610 --> 00:19:08.930
Um, want me to wipe your tears?

00:19:08.930 --> 00:19:09.420
No.

00:19:11.970 --> 00:19:15.420
You know, since I left Wonderland,

00:19:15.420 --> 00:19:17.880
I found lots of new things I like.

00:19:20.890 --> 00:19:22.680
I've met so many people,

00:19:22.680 --> 00:19:26.800
and found things that are 
delicious, fun, and exciting,

00:19:26.800 --> 00:19:30.900
and things that won't leave my 
mind, even if they're annoying.

00:19:30.900 --> 00:19:34.340
Maybe all the things that 
make me feel frazzled

00:19:34.340 --> 00:19:36.110
are actually all wrong

00:19:36.660 --> 00:19:38.750
and aren't needed at all.

00:19:40.120 --> 00:19:41.780
I can't prove it,

00:19:41.780 --> 00:19:44.280
but I do need them!

00:19:44.840 --> 00:19:47.950
That's why I decided to insist 
that they <i>are</i> necessary!

00:19:48.490 --> 00:19:53.960
So hearing you say it'd be better 
if you weren't around is just...

00:19:53.960 --> 00:19:57.010
I mean, it's kind of...

00:19:59.330 --> 00:20:02.920
You really are a mysterious girl.

00:20:03.430 --> 00:20:05.220
Really? I'm mysterious?

00:20:06.460 --> 00:20:07.890
Huh? What are you doing?

00:20:07.890 --> 00:20:10.640
My Sanae does this to me a lot.

00:20:11.090 --> 00:20:12.270
"Your" Sanae?

00:20:12.270 --> 00:20:13.020
Yeah.

00:20:13.600 --> 00:20:17.230
All the people I know are big.

00:20:18.060 --> 00:20:21.940
So even when I talk about stuff 
like this, they don't listen.

00:20:21.940 --> 00:20:24.550
I always feel so frazzled,

00:20:24.550 --> 00:20:27.770
but they just say I'm doing great, 
or I'll understand when I'm older.

00:20:29.460 --> 00:20:31.100
How old are you?

00:20:31.100 --> 00:20:33.190
Uh, I don't know.

00:20:33.190 --> 00:20:34.850
Between eight and ten.

00:20:34.850 --> 00:20:37.700
We might be around the same age, then.

00:20:37.700 --> 00:20:40.280
Really? I think I'm older than you!

00:20:40.280 --> 00:20:42.670
No, I'm older than you.

00:20:42.670 --> 00:20:44.180
No, I am!

00:20:47.070 --> 00:20:49.770
Can I stay like this for a little bit?

00:20:52.120 --> 00:20:55.900
When I was little, my mom 
held me like this a lot.

00:20:58.120 --> 00:21:00.700
I introduced myself,

00:21:00.700 --> 00:21:02.860
but everyone laughed 
and said I was weird.

00:21:02.860 --> 00:21:05.240
When the teacher said

00:21:05.240 --> 00:21:08.020
I didn't have to introduce myself 
when I enter the classroom,

00:21:08.020 --> 00:21:10.580
they all laughed at me again!

00:21:10.580 --> 00:21:12.550
And then... And then...

00:21:12.550 --> 00:21:14.930
You don't need to worry about that.

00:21:14.930 --> 00:21:18.770
You introduced yourself, 
just like I told you to.

00:21:20.760 --> 00:21:24.130
Little crybaby Ha-chan, 
I'll have to squeeze you.

00:21:24.740 --> 00:21:26.600
<i>Do you remember, Mom?</i>

00:21:27.110 --> 00:21:30.870
<i>I was sad then,</i>

00:21:30.870 --> 00:21:32.660
<i>but so happy.</i>

00:21:32.660 --> 00:21:34.600
<i>I felt truly blessed.</i>

00:21:37.360 --> 00:21:39.360
<i>It's just like back then.</i>

00:21:42.850 --> 00:21:44.860
<i>I can hear her heartbeat.</i>

00:21:46.110 --> 00:21:47.530
Listen...

00:21:47.530 --> 00:21:49.950
I'd like to see my mom once more.

00:21:50.430 --> 00:21:51.980
Will you help me?

00:21:52.600 --> 00:21:53.660
Yeah.

00:21:56.280 --> 00:21:57.480
Thanks.

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.020
Next Episode 
I'm Home

00:23:36.420 --> 00:23:37.520
I'm Home.
